				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2203795&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606207881" alt="Kalinin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2203795)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;" >Kalinin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1472580177 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Aug 2016 18:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2580930">
									

<p>In terms of nuclear gamesmanship, I don't understand this at all. This acknowledges the existence of Dead Hand, which is a second-strike fail-deadly deterrence mechanism, and states that it's intended to be used in conjunction with it. But those kinds of deterrents are only there as insurance that if the other party takes out your leadership and command structure in a first strike, that you'll still be able to retaliate and effectively end the world. So this is intended to kill everyone.</p>
<p>But why on earth is it being presented as a GRU-P false flag meant to prolong the existence of the Soviet Union? That makes no sense at all. There's no need to trouble with a false flag operation if the end result is going to be a world-destroying nuclear exchange. At that point, what does it matter who started it? That's also ignoring the fact that the Soviet Union is unlikely to still be around if <em>everyone in the world is dead.</em></p>
<p>Even in the highly unlikely event that GRU-P is so suicidally unwilling to plan ahead for what might happen in the event of a nuclear strike on a world superpower, and they were all like &quot;yes, this will work perfectly,&quot; the <em>infinite tactical nukes</em> that follow will certainly finish the job for whatever is left. You've basically removed the interesting implications to be fished out mutual assured destruction and replaced with a straight doomsday device.</p>

							</div>

								
					
