														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2580943">
									

<p>I guess I'm still not understanding then, because the false flag operation is using nuclear weapons, and will therefore incite nuclear war. That's literally a suicidal course of action, one that was avoided by even the most aggressive regimes on both sides during the Cold War. And infinite bomber fleets attacking NATO is still going to result in worldwide devastation.</p>
<p>The GOC doing the stereotypical GOC thing doesn't even really change anything. Whether nukes are being lobbed at Moscow or Washington, the results are going to be the same in the end. I guess that's what's tripping me up about this; it seems to be written with the idea that a one-sided nuclear strike between the US and the USSR was somehow possible and desirable enough that someone thought it was a good idea to pursue. That goes beyond my suspension of disbelief.</p>

