			<div class="content" id="post-content-2580951">
									

<p>I guess it's a little unclear - the false-flag bits, and the nuclear bits, are totally separate parts of the same system. The false flag part was to make UK-looking bombers attack a Warsaw Pact city, leading to war. Whether that was a nuclear strike or not depends on how ballsy they're feeling.</p>
<p>Later on, they decided they could extend the system to act as a lethal, unavoidable second strike that would flatten the west in the event the Soviet are caught on the pointy end of a decapitating strike.</p>
<p>Both were functions of the same system, but never intended to be used together in any capacity.</p>
<p>When the GOC wrecked the system, the system breaks down and things start working not as intended.</p>
<p>Now that you mention it it's a little unclear, but I'm not sure how I can alleviate. You're the first one to bring it up.</p>

