														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2819060">
									

<p>Personally, this entire article seems half-baked and rushed. There are typos and spelling/grammar errors scattered throughout the entire thing, the tone SEEMS fine, but it just feels incredibly bland and kind of incomplete.</p>
<p>Also, what's with the weird not-redaction of ONE part of ONE date in the timeline? Why un-redact the month for only that one entry? At least it's a new form of bad redaction, I guess.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Some&nbsp;specific&nbsp;issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">The source of SCP-2326-1 instances is currently unknown</span>. Removal of the source of instances of SCP-2326-1 is ongoing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can't find ANY reference in this article for this. Where do they come from and how are we removing the source?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Foundation Site 2326-A is sited at a derelict radar station on the outskirts of Tula, Russia. A research group of Foundation researchers should work to restore SCP-2326-2 to working order to remove the threat that 2326-Tango events pose.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You actually never say what 2326-2 is. Much like -3, we can infer it from, literally, the paragraphs they're in, which is at least decent writing, but in this kind of document they should be explicitly spelled out, ESPECIALLY in the containment procedures.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Surviving instances are unable to answer relevant questions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Prove it. Where's the documentation?</p>
<blockquote>
<h1><span>Internal Document 2326-1 Request for Assistance Level 3/2326 Clearance Required</span></h1>
</blockquote>
<p>This document seems very, very poorly formatted/written. Once again, props on managing to explain what this is from context, but WE SHOULD NOT REQUIRE CONTEXT for things like what a document on the file is - they should be stated.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I feel like this is pretty bad - it's a bit bland and uninspired, and on top of that feels wildly incomplete. I don't really think this should even have made it onto the main site in this stage - it feels like it's still in a draft.</p>

							</div>

								
					
